  {
   "type": "worked_example",
   "title": "Example 7 · Turns around: $Y=|X|$ (Tutorial 6 Q4)",
   "prompt": "$X\\sim U(-1,1)$. Find the PDF of $Y=|X|$, then $P(|X|>\\tfrac12)$.",
   "steps": [
    {
     "explanation": "**Spot:** $|x|$ turns around at $0$. An interval again.",
     "latex": ""
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Range:** $|x|$ on $[-1,1]$ runs from $0$ to $1$.",
     "latex": "0\\le Y\\le1"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Rewrite.**",
     "latex": "|X|\\le y\\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad -y\\le X\\le y"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Accumulate:** length $2y$, height $\\tfrac12$.",
     "latex": "F_Y(y)=2y\\cdot\\frac12=y"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Differentiate.**",
     "latex": "f_Y(y)=1,\\qquad 0<y<1"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "The probability is one minus the CDF.",
     "latex": "P\\big(|X|>\\frac12\\big)=1-F_Y\\big(\\frac12\\big)=1-\\frac12=\\frac12"
    }
   ],
   "answer": "$f_Y(y)=1$ on $(0,1)$, so $|X|\\sim U(0,1)$; $P(|X|>\\tfrac12)=\\tfrac12$.",
   "citations": [
    {
     "source_id": "8b50801c-193d-4e1e-92f4-d54dc3a7332b",
     "version": 1,
     "chunk_id": "35f99245-aa41-4957-9ed0-1ca171c35e49"
    }
   ],
   "id": "4b710ab1-ea35-5244-9a68-17b77703c552"
  },
  {
   "type": "worked_example",
   "title": "Example 8 · A Gaussian through a line: $Y=2X+1$",
   "prompt": "$X\\sim N(0,1)$. Write $F_Y(y)$ for $Y=2X+1$ using $\\Phi$. What distribution is $Y$? Find $P(Y>3)$.",
   "steps": [
    {
     "explanation": "**Spot:** slope $2>0$, so $g$ only goes up. **Read off** $a$ and $b$ for the $aX+b$ formula.",
     "latex": "a=2,\\qquad b=1"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Rewrite.**",
     "latex": "2X+1\\le y\\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad X\\le\\frac{y-1}{2}"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Accumulate:** $X$ is standard normal, so $F_X=\\Phi$.",
     "latex": "F_Y(y)=\\Phi\\Big(\\frac{y-1}{2}\\Big)"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "That’s the CDF of a Gaussian with $\\mu=1$, $\\sigma=2$.",
     "latex": "Y\\sim N(1,\\,4)"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "Complement, then the table: $\\Phi(1)=0.8413$.",
     "latex": "P(Y>3)=1-\\Phi\\Big(\\frac{3-1}{2}\\Big)=1-\\Phi(1)\\approx0.1587"
    }
   ],
   "answer": "$F_Y(y)=\\Phi\\left(\\tfrac{y-1}{2}\\right)$, so $Y\\sim N(1,4)$; $P(Y>3)\\approx 0.1587$.",
   "citations": [],
   "id": "28588640-ba30-5186-86eb-8f54d0413327"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 1,
   "text": "Extras: flat pieces (mixed Y) and a shortcut formula",
   "citations": [],
   "id": "44e491c4-a892-5306-831b-080464b29e10"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "**When $g$ goes flat.** Clipping, a rectifier, a limiter, a timeout: $\\max\\{X,0\\}$, $\\min\\{X,1\\}$. A flat piece at height $c$ sends a whole interval of $X$ to the single value $c$. So $Y=c$ has real chance, and $F_Y$ **jumps** there:",
   "citations": [],
   "id": "c011a578-a756-5eb1-b9d7-c581f659644c"
  },
  {
   "type": "equation",
   "latex": "P(Y=c)=P\\big(X\\text{ is in the flat part}\\big)",
   "display": true,
   "citations": [
    {
     "source_id": "8fc07b50-0ad8-4dd1-9994-4284ef5b512d",
     "version": 1,
     "chunk_id": "2eed7acb-8ac6-4738-99c3-478135a51df2"
    }
   ],
   "id": "c267b53f-6817-5225-b9b4-3523de397fbd"
  },
  {
   "type": "list",
   "items": [
    "**Range:** as always.",
    "**Jump:** one per flat piece, sized $P(X$ in that piece$)$.",
    "**Accumulate** everywhere else, as in Topic 2.",
    "**Spot:** jumps plus a slope means $Y$ is **mixed**."
   ],
   "ordered": true,
   "citations": [],
   "id": "84130a61-ce78-5e16-a746-e102f5ba5b79"
  },
  {
   "type": "worked_example",
   "title": "Example 9 · Flat piece: a half-wave rectifier $Y=\\max\\{X,0\\}$ (Lecture 14)",
   "prompt": "$X\\sim U(-1,1)$. Find the CDF of $Y=\\max\\{X,0\\}$. What type is $Y$?",
   "steps": [
    {
     "explanation": "**Range:** negative $X$ become $0$, positive $X$ stay.",
     "latex": "0\\le Y\\le1"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Jump** at $0$: the flat part is every $X\\le0$.",
     "latex": "P(Y=0)=P(X\\le0)=\\frac12"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Accumulate**, $0\\le y\\le1$: $\\max\\{X,0\\}\\le y$ just means $X\\le y$.",
     "latex": "F_Y(y)=P(X\\le y)=\\frac{y+1}{2}"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "Put the pieces together.",
     "latex": "F_Y(y)=\\begin{cases}0,&y<0\\\\ \\dfrac{y+1}{2},&0\\le y\\le1\\\\ 1,&y>1\\end{cases}"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Spot:** a jump of $\\tfrac12$ at $0$, then a slope.",
     "latex": "\\text{mixed}"
    }
   ],
   "answer": "Mixed: $P(Y=0)=\\tfrac12$, plus density $\\tfrac12$ on $(0,1)$.",
   "citations": [
    {
     "source_id": "8fc07b50-0ad8-4dd1-9994-4284ef5b512d",
     "version": 1,
     "chunk_id": "d9617600-27dd-4cf7-9e1d-8e6ceb5a6445"
    },
    {
     "source_id": "8fc07b50-0ad8-4dd1-9994-4284ef5b512d",
     "version": 1,
     "chunk_id": "1d66e547-c5e8-41a6-bcfa-a351228e8590"
    }
   ],
   "id": "cda938aa-9158-57fa-8aa7-b5096069980b"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "**What the jump looks like:**\n\n```graph\ntitle \"$F_Y$ for $Y=\\max\\{X,0\\}$: the flat piece becomes a jump\"\nx -0.6 1.5 label=\"$y$\" height=200\ny 0 1.12 label=\"$F_Y(y)$\"\nsegment \"-0.6\" \"0\" \"0\" \"0\" color=2\ncurve \"(x+1)/2\" from=0 to=1 color=2\nsegment \"1\" \"1\" \"1.5\" \"1\" color=2\npoint \"0\" \"0.5\" color=2\nsegment \"0\" \"0\" \"0\" \"0.5\" color=2 dash\ntext \"0.42\" \"0.25\" \"jump $\\tfrac12=P(Y=0)$\"\n```",
   "citations": [],
   "id": "6d78ef13-a781-5a00-b46c-78c0de5d4d5d"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "**The shortcut formula** (not from the lectures: use it to check your answer). It skips the CDF. It works when $g$ only goes up **or** only goes down:",
   "citations": [],
   "id": "51603e5a-ce9e-5313-a8e8-0f2b45da189e"
  },
  {
   "type": "equation",
   "latex": "f_Y(y)=f_X\\big(g^{-1}(y)\\big)\\cdot\\Big|\\frac{d}{dy}g^{-1}(y)\\Big|",
   "display": true,
   "citations": [],
   "id": "0c998f27-5c4b-5bd0-9e0b-71ad7dd6b226"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "When $g$ turns around, add one term per $x$ that lands on $y$:",
   "citations": [],
   "id": "b036e932-8604-5f11-bce7-63da78ee2873"
  },
  {
   "type": "equation",
   "latex": "\\begin{gathered}Y=X^2:\\quad f_Y(y)=\\frac{f_X(\\sqrt y)+f_X(-\\sqrt y)}{2\\sqrt y}\\\\ Y=|X|:\\quad f_Y(y)=f_X(y)+f_X(-y)\\end{gathered}\\qquad y>0",
   "display": true,
   "citations": [],
   "id": "7a21764a-9324-57f1-869c-51849683507a"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "**A line keeps the family:** Gaussian in, Gaussian out. Uniform in, uniform out (push the two ends through).",
   "citations": [],
   "id": "174a8c6e-2724-541b-a0ff-fd80b37fdfe0"
  },
  {
   "type": "equation",
   "latex": "X\\sim N(\\mu,\\sigma^2)\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad aX+b\\sim N(a\\mu+b,\\ a^2\\sigma^2)",
   "display": true,
   "citations": [],
   "id": "baa41084-4bb7-5346-8889-6987f5567c35"
  },
  {
   "type": "worked_example",
   "title": "Example 10 · Shortcut check: $Y=X^3$ and $Y=X^2$",
   "prompt": "Check the Topic 2 answers for $X\\sim U(-1,1)$ with the shortcut formulas.",
   "steps": [
