   "type": "practice_problem",
   "title": "Question 4 · Continuous $Y$, goes up · $e^X$ · Tutorial 6 Q3",
   "difficulty": "introductory",
   "origin": "source",
   "prompt": "$X\\sim U(0,1)$. Find the CDF and PDF of $Y=e^X$.",
   "solution": "",
   "steps": [
    {
     "explanation": "**Spot:** $e^x$ only goes up → $F_Y(y)=F_X(g^{-1}(y))$.",
     "latex": ""
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Range:** $e^0=1$ to $e^1=e$.",
     "latex": "1\\le Y\\le e"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Rewrite:** undo the $e$.",
     "latex": "e^X\\le y\\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad X\\le\\ln y"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Accumulate:** $F_X(x)=x$ on $[0,1]$.",
     "latex": "F_Y(y)=\\ln y,\\qquad 1\\le y\\le e"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Differentiate.**",
     "latex": "f_Y(y)=\\frac1y,\\qquad 1<y<e"
    }
   ],
   "answer": "$F_Y=\\ln y$ on $[1,e]$ ($0$ below, $1$ above); $f_Y(y)=\\dfrac1y$ for $1<y<e$.",
