   "type": "practice_problem",
   "title": "Question 5 · Continuous $Y$ · a line, up and down · Lecture 15",
   "difficulty": "introductory",
   "origin": "source",
   "prompt": "$X\\sim U(0,2)$. Find the CDF and PDF of (a) $Y=3X+1$, (b) $W=4-2X$. What distributions are they?",
   "solution": "",
   "steps": [
    {
     "explanation": "(a) **Spot:** slope $3>0$, only goes up. **Range:** $x=0\\to1$, $x=2\\to7$.",
     "latex": "1\\le Y\\le7"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Rewrite.**",
     "latex": "3X+1\\le y\\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad X\\le\\frac{y-1}{3}"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Accumulate:** $F_X(x)=\\tfrac x2$.",
     "latex": "F_Y(y)=\\frac{y-1}{6},\\qquad 1\\le y\\le7"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Differentiate.**",
     "latex": "f_Y(y)=\\frac16\\ \\text{ on }(1,7)\\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad Y\\sim U(1,7)"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "(b) **Spot:** slope $-2<0$, only goes down: the $\\le$ flips. **Range:** $x=0\\to4$, $x=2\\to0$.",
     "latex": "0\\le W\\le4"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Rewrite:** subtract 4, divide by $-2$ (flip).",
     "latex": "4-2X\\le w\\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad X\\ge\\frac{4-w}{2}"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Accumulate:** $P(X\\ge t)=1-\\tfrac t2$.",
     "latex": "F_W(w)=1-\\frac{4-w}{4}=\\frac w4,\\qquad 0\\le w\\le4"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Differentiate.**",
     "latex": "f_W(w)=\\frac14\\ \\text{ on }(0,4)\\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad W\\sim U(0,4)"
    }
   ],
   "answer": "(a) $F_Y=\\tfrac{y-1}{6}$, $Y\\sim U(1,7)$ (b) $F_W=\\tfrac w4$, $W\\sim U(0,4)$",
   "citations": [
    {
     "source_id": "02aff1ce-de48-4c04-b61d-906e7ad59715",
     "version": 1,
     "chunk_id": "28df4f3d-382b-4027-b8f5-4cc69b31d12d"
    }
   ],
   "id": "1cdfa4db-ef90-555a-aa66-ffa96cff1532"
