  {
   "type": "practice_problem",
   "title": "Question 6 · Continuous $Y$, goes down · decreasing $g$",
   "difficulty": "intermediate",
   "origin": "original",
   "prompt": "(a) $X\\sim$ Exp$(\\lambda)$. Find the CDF and PDF of $Y=-2X+3$. (b) $X\\sim U(0,1)$. Find the CDF and PDF of $Y=-\\ln X$.",
   "solution": "",
   "steps": [
    {
     "explanation": "(a) **Spot:** slope $-2$, only goes down → the $\\le$ flips. **Range:** $X\\ge0$, so $Y=3-2X\\le3$.",
     "latex": "Y\\le3"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Rewrite:** subtract 3, divide by $-2$ (flip).",
     "latex": "-2X+3\\le y\\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad X\\ge\\frac{3-y}{2}"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Accumulate:** the exponential tail, $P(X\\ge x)=e^{-\\lambda x}$.",
     "latex": "F_Y(y)=e^{-\\lambda(3-y)/2},\\qquad y\\le3"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Differentiate** (chain rule: the inside has slope $\\tfrac\\lambda2$).",
     "latex": "f_Y(y)=\\frac{\\lambda}{2}\\,e^{-\\lambda(3-y)/2},\\qquad y<3"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "(b) **Spot:** $-\\ln x$ only goes down → the $\\le$ flips. **Range:** $X\\in(0,1)$, so $-\\ln X\\in(0,\\infty)$.",
     "latex": "Y>0"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Rewrite:** multiply by $-1$ (flip), then undo the $\\ln$.",
     "latex": "-\\ln X\\le y\\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad X\\ge e^{-y}"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Accumulate:** $P(X\\ge t)=1-t$.",
     "latex": "F_Y(y)=1-e^{-y},\\qquad y\\ge0"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Differentiate.** That’s the Exp$(1)$ PDF.",
     "latex": "f_Y(y)=e^{-y},\\qquad y>0"
    }
   ],
   "answer": "(a) $F_Y=e^{-\\lambda(3-y)/2}$ for $y\\le3$, $f_Y=\\tfrac\\lambda2e^{-\\lambda(3-y)/2}$ (b) $F_Y=1-e^{-y}$, $f_Y=e^{-y}$: $Y\\sim$ Exp$(1)$.",
